1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:03,480
EPISODE 8: A WORLD BUILT ON HYPOCRISY

3
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,909
That'll be 28,300 won.

4
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:17,869
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

5
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,622
- You're all set.
- Thank you.

6
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,250
Have a nice day.

7
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:57,701
BROTHER-IN-LAW
DID YOU EAT LUNCH YET?

8
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:02,455
Why here?
We could've eaten something better.

9
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:04,708
If you come to Busan,
a pork gukbap is a must.

10
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:07,418
Actually, I was craving it.

11
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:08,794
I get to eat it, thanks to you.

12
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:09,879
Eat up.

13
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,632
You too.

14
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:20,057
What is this?

15
00:02:20,724 --> 00:02:22,558
A-yeong's tutoring is expensive.

16
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:23,852
I wanted to help out.

17
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:27,356
It costs more to live in Seoul.

18
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:31,776
We don't have to pay rent,
and we both work

19
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:34,528
- so we're all right.
- A-yeong is my niece.

20
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,822
I want to do this.

21
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,659
Then we'll put it to good use.

22
00:02:39,368 --> 00:02:41,035
Thank you as always, Eun-tae.

23
00:02:41,036 --> 00:02:42,329
It's nothing.

24
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:48,626
How is my brother doing lately?

25
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,504
Well...

26
00:02:50,921 --> 00:02:52,631
I'm sure he's doing fine.

27
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,010
He works nights,
so we rarely see each other.

28
00:02:58,136 --> 00:03:00,681
Well, I feel bad for him.

29
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:04,518
He used to be so successful,
but now he seems so dejected.

30
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:07,269
Back in the day

31
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:10,982
Gong Eun-seok was synonymous
with Busan's fashion scene.

32
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:16,070
He was the first person
to bring items trending in Japan

33
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:17,947
to the Busan market.

34
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:21,242
Those shabby-looking clothes
sold so well.

35
00:03:21,243 --> 00:03:22,786
Yes, I remember now.

36
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:25,163
The neighborhood went crazy
back then.

37
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:27,457
After he became successful

38
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,836
he bought me Korean beef
to celebrate my college admission.

39
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,796
That was my first time
having Korean beef.

40
00:03:33,797 --> 00:03:36,049
I had no clue it was that good.
It was delicious.

41
00:03:36,425 --> 00:03:38,342
Thanks to Eun-seok

42
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:41,638
I still have a habit of eating that
whenever something good happens.

43
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,433
Was it the barbecue place
in Seomyeon?

44
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:47,226
Yes, have you ever been?

45
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,478
That's where he seduced me.

46
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:52,107
So the mere mention of Korean beef
makes me shudder.

47
00:03:57,988 --> 00:03:59,156
Actually...

48
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:03,326
Eun-seok asked me
for money yesterday.

49
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:04,828
Again?

50
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:08,039
I'm so sorry, Eun-tae.

51
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:11,001
What will I do with that man?

52
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:14,379
That's not why I'm bringing it up.

53
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:18,508
He said he wanted to start a business

54
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:21,094
but I told him
I couldn't give him the money.

55
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,598
In my opinion,
I don't think it'll do well.

56
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:29,060
But I could be wrong.

57
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:31,563
His business might end up doing well.

58
00:04:32,314 --> 00:04:35,817
So in the hope that I'm wrong

59
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:39,404
I want to help him out how I can.

60
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:41,865
With that being said

61
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:44,576
I hope you can accept this money.

62
00:04:49,748 --> 00:04:51,291
Don't hate my brother too much.

63
00:04:53,043 --> 00:04:55,045
He may seem a bit lousy right now

64
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:57,422
but I still think

65
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,842
he's a great person.

66
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:04,304
Gosh.

67
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:06,306
He's a lucky man.

68
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:10,976
Even in his lousy state,
his brother thinks he's great.

69
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:14,189
At one time,
he was the coolest person I knew.

70
00:05:15,232 --> 00:05:17,317
But right now,
I think you're the coolest.

71
00:05:17,943 --> 00:05:20,319
Me? Why is that?

72
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,113
You haven't given up on him.

73
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,825
Gosh, what are you saying?

74
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:27,077
Hurry up and eat.

75
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,322
INCOMING CALL
TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

76
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:09,119
Thank you.

77
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:13,665
How's work these days?

78
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:17,294
You know how it goes.

79
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,296
It's always the same.

80
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,674
Sure, work is all the same.

81
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,428
So how long will you stay
at Hongsung?

82
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,017
I haven't thought about it.

83
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:34,477
How about some food for thought?

84
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:37,355
I believe
I already rejected your offer.

85
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:39,899
Our company merged.

86
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,026
I'm no longer the CEO.

87
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:43,695
Does that mean

88
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:46,072
you've joined a bigger company?

89
00:06:51,286 --> 00:06:52,662
An article will come out tomorrow.

90
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,332
It'll send quite a shock
through the market.

91
00:07:01,296 --> 00:07:02,923
Korea Branch Manager of CGM?

92
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:05,592
CGM is entering the Korean market.

93
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:08,344
Based on our predictions

94
00:07:08,345 --> 00:07:11,555
all small and medium-sized brand
controllers in Korea will disappear.

95
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:12,681
It looks like

96
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:15,059
Hongsung will survive
for the next three years

97
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,978
but revenue will be cut by one-third.

98
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:18,647
All right.

99
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:22,275
So as Head Brand Manager

100
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:25,695
you'd have a six-figure salary
of at least 100,000 dollars.

101
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,155
How's that?

102
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:29,115
Is that enough
to start thinking about it?

103
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:51,554
Jeez.

104
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:57,852
What's the reason?

105
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,980
Do I have to tell you that?

106
00:08:00,397 --> 00:08:03,066
CGM is the best brand controller
in North America.

107
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:05,859
Hongsung is a corner store
compared to them.

108
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,528
If you stay there

109
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:09,613
all you'll get is early retirement.

110
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:10,615
So why?

111
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,912
When making a decision

112
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:19,416
one should be
most cautious about money.

113
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,002
My worth remains the same.

114
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:23,920
I should be suspicious
if I'm offered more money.

115
00:08:26,006 --> 00:08:27,340
Don't you think

116
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:30,135
your current worth
is being underestimated?

117
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:34,180
Some people might be getting paid
more than they're worth.

118
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,150
I understand.

119
00:08:45,859 --> 00:08:48,445
But I guarantee

120
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:51,698
you'll regret this moment.

121
00:08:55,744 --> 00:08:57,954
You shouldn't be doing this,
Mr. Jeong.

122
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:02,584
Do you think

123
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:05,712
you did me a favor or something?

124
00:09:07,672 --> 00:09:09,716
I considered it an insult.

125
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,219
There's something you got wrong.

126
00:09:14,429 --> 00:09:17,557
Do you think Mr. Jeong
will be grateful for what you did?

127
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:24,396
Are you saying you want revenge
for that insult?

128
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:25,440
No.

129
00:09:25,774 --> 00:09:27,525
I'm just doing my job.

130
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:31,404
CGM called to say they were looking
for a Korea Branch Manager.

131
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:35,157
Someone from Hongsung
or a large enough Korean company

132
00:09:35,158 --> 00:09:38,243
who has enough influence
as a sole proprietor

133
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:39,788
but lacks the funds.

134
00:09:40,872 --> 00:09:42,916
I just happened to align
with the terms.

135
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,168
Who cares about trivial revenge?

136
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:47,378
It's just work.

137
00:09:54,344 --> 00:09:56,096
100 DAYS OF PRAYER
FOR SUCCESS ON THE 2027 CSAT

138
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:42,600
Mr. Jang.

139
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,575
What kind of team leader
surprises their boss

140
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:01,995
on a spiritual retreat
during the holiday break?

141
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:03,454
You scared me to death.

142
00:11:04,581 --> 00:11:05,582
I'm sorry, sir.

143
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:08,877
Anyway, how did you find me?

144
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:12,087
You weren't answering any of my calls

145
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:13,214
so I called your house.

146
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,509
Well done.

147
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,847
So is there something wrong?

148
00:11:21,806 --> 00:11:22,807
By any chance

149
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:26,394
have you heard any news
about Mr. Jeong's company?

150
00:11:27,896 --> 00:11:29,856
Jeong Seon-hyuk's company? No.

151
00:11:31,274 --> 00:11:33,776
CGM acquired his company.

152
00:11:34,736 --> 00:11:35,737
CGM?

153
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:38,238
Are you talking
about the CGM we know?

154
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,616
Yes, they plan to enter Korea.

155
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,368
Mr. Jeong is their
Korea Branch Manager.

156
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:49,959
Why are you telling me this now?

157
00:11:51,294 --> 00:11:53,046
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

158
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:54,713
Come on.

159
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:56,799
You should've started with that.

160
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,760
Well, there's a certain flow
to conversations...

161
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:01,929
Gosh, what is wrong with you?

162
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:03,514
You're such a strange guy.

163
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:06,726
I mean, don't you know
what's important?

164
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:09,145
Jeez.

165
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,820
CGM DECLARES KOREA EXPANSION,
DOMESTIC COMPANIES ON HIGH ALERT

166
00:12:29,666 --> 00:12:31,376
BELOVED BY HOLLYWOOD,
OAULD WILL BE LAUNCHED BY CGM

167
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,807
WHO WILL SURVIVE THE FASHION MARKET'S
GLOBAL BATTLEFIELD?

168
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:56,025
KOREA BRANCH MANAGER
JEONG SEON-HYUK

169
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:08,955
CGM'S AMBITIOUS KOREA BRANCH MANAGER
JEONG SEON-HYUK

170
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:17,213
Jeong Seon-hyuk
must be over the moon.

171
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:20,174
The fact that articles
have been published

172
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:24,012
means they've already finished talks
with brands and malls.

173
00:13:26,723 --> 00:13:28,348
It appears they were

174
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:31,184
strategically laying the groundwork
at the three biggest malls.

175
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,644
Right as the articles dropped

176
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:34,314
they distributed
their entire brand list

177
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,649
to shopping complexes and outlets.

178
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:39,986
Did you get the list of brands
CGM is launching?

179
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:45,615
There are around 300 global brands,
as well as some domestic brands.

180
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:50,413
It basically includes all the brands
they control in North America.

181
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:54,292
They've set the table
and are telling retailers to eat up.

182
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:57,670
Based on Oauld's entry contract

183
00:13:58,338 --> 00:14:00,256
it looks like CGM sacrificed
their profit margin.

184
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,883
They're essentially
trying to eliminate

185
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:04,510
all the domestic brand controllers.

186
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:08,597
If we fight amongst ourselves

187
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:11,809
malls and shopping complexes
will have the upper hand.

188
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,311
And once the weak are eliminated

189
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:17,398
CGM will monopolize
nearly half of the market.

190
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:19,941
Yes, since the early stage
of their expansion

191
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:22,195
their intention seems to be
full domination.

192
00:14:28,493 --> 00:14:32,288
Ma'am, Paradi Mall is requesting
an amendment to the Aileye contract.

193
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:35,665
- Aileye just renewed their contract.
- Right.

194
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:37,459
If we don't renew the contract

195
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,462
they're even willing to pay
the penalty.

196
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:42,172
When Paradi Mall first opened

197
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:44,801
they clung onto us and begged us
to help them open stores...

198
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:46,594
Didn't they?

199
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,599
Since they begged us

200
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:54,227
now they want us to beg them.

201
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:57,021
I doubt they're the only ones.

202
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,316
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes, ma'am.

203
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:04,152
Gather a list of stores and brands
where complications have arisen

204
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,905
and give me an initial report
by the end of the day.

205
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:07,239
Yes, ma'am.

206
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,365
Mr. Gong.

207
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:09,951
Consult with the Legal Team.

208
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:13,746
Compare the size of penalties
and sales projections and brief me.

209
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:17,708
You should at least do that
to ease your conscience.

210
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:21,379
Yes, ma'am.

211
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,094
Goodbye, ma'am.

212
00:15:29,554 --> 00:15:31,722
LOIRE OUTLET
SCAN-BASED TRADING SALES CONTRACT

213
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,444
Hello.

214
00:15:49,824 --> 00:15:50,825
Gosh.

215
00:15:51,826 --> 00:15:53,286
You should eat a proper meal.

216
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:56,413
What is it?

217
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:57,914
Do you need to report
on the penalty scale?

218
00:15:57,915 --> 00:15:58,999
Yeah.

219
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,375
JIN HAE-JU

220
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:01,419
Go back and wait.

221
00:16:01,752 --> 00:16:03,463
I have so many brands to review.

222
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:06,549
Right, then should I go back?

223
00:16:14,891 --> 00:16:16,516
You probably didn't eat, either.

224
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:18,060
When you're busy,
this is better than a meal.

225
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,068
Just go back and wait.

226
00:16:28,029 --> 00:16:29,238
This is really good.

227
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:33,868
Let's talk outside.

228
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,995
Are you sure? Aren't you busy?

229
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:38,581
If you knew that,
you shouldn't have come here.

230
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:42,209
The managing director is inside.

231
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,544
- Let's leave.
- Okay.

232
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:55,305
The managing director
doesn't like you.

233
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:57,433
Says you make problems
out of nothing.

234
00:16:57,767 --> 00:16:58,975
That's understandable.

235
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:01,187
You change contracts as you please.

236
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,272
There's also Mr. Jeong's case.

237
00:17:03,773 --> 00:17:04,940
We dealt with him

238
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:07,567
but then you helped him,
which led to all of this.

239
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,569
You're right.

240
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:11,279
- Gosh, you really...
- So

241
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,616
when can I get
the full amount of penalties?

242
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,077
- Approximately.
- I don't know, either.

243
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:19,663
There's no guarantee we can get
the exact amount listed in contracts.

244
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:21,831
We have to compare
the time spent on litigation

245
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:24,168
and the actual amount we can receive.

246
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:26,837
With all of that, when can I get it?

247
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:28,548
- Hey, you...
- Hae-ju.

248
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:32,927
I get that it's a struggle,
and that you're upset.

249
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,513
But we still have to work.

250
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,307
I need the timeline so I can prepare.

251
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:40,100
You're really...

252
00:17:40,101 --> 00:17:43,311
If every brand under CGM
wants to terminate their contract

253
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:45,355
the penalty amount in the contract

254
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:46,607
plus compensation for damages

255
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,150
totals 280 billion won.

256
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,194
Since it'd be a one-sided termination

257
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:54,072
if we assume it won't go to court
and they'll pay up without a fight

258
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:55,366
the amount would be similar.

259
00:17:56,284 --> 00:17:59,494
Before the end of the day,
at least give me an estimate.

260
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:02,081
I'll report it for now
and follow up again later.

261
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,960
I'll get it to you by 5 p.m.
Happy now?

262
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:08,212
Thank you.

263
00:18:08,838 --> 00:18:11,339
But if I were on their legal team

264
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,049
even if it's a one-sided termination

265
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,719
I wouldn't tell them to pay up
without a fight.

266
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:18,014
I'd nitpick and do everything I could
to make both parties at fault.

267
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:20,933
Speaking of which...

268
00:18:21,976 --> 00:18:24,519
Malls have more than enough power
to find a way

269
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,480
to make contract termination
both parties' fault.

270
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:30,151
So if they agree to pay the penalty
without putting up a fight

271
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,111
that money is coming from CGM.

272
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:36,741
I'm the one suffering.

273
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,284
Mr. Oh.

274
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:40,244
Can we talk for a moment?

275
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:41,662
- Me?
- Just a moment.

276
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:47,168
Mr. Oh.

277
00:18:47,918 --> 00:18:49,879
Has Mr. Jeong offered you a job?

278
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:51,672
No.

279
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:53,924
Why, did you get an offer?

280
00:18:54,717 --> 00:18:55,800
Yes.

281
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,303
That bastard...

282
00:18:58,429 --> 00:18:59,430
Would you accept if you got one?

283
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,598
No, I wouldn't.

284
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:03,850
But I'm annoyed
that he didn't even offer.

285
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:04,976
What about you, Ms. Joo?

286
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:06,145
Will you accept?

287
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,189
Yes, I'm going to accept it.

288
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:11,442
He told me to bring you.

289
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:13,861
- Me?
- Yeah.

290
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,446
You see how things are going here.

291
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:17,656
It's hopeless.

292
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:18,948
Let's go together.

293
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:21,410
Do I start right away, then?

294
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,037
I can quit right now.

295
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:26,123
Don't quit yet.

296
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:30,378
Why don't you stay here
and keep us in the loop?

297
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:35,675
Be a mole?

298
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:49,813
Well, things are hectic
for all of us.

299
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:52,024
Did you hear anything
from the brand's end?

300
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:55,361
We haven't heard much, either.

301
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:58,155
All right, we'll talk soon. Bye.

302
00:19:58,614 --> 00:19:59,864
- Mr. Yang.
- Yes?

303
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:02,367
Should I mark Richard Hansen
as backing out as well?

304
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:03,785
They do have a monopoly in Asia...

305
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:04,787
- Hang on.
- Sure.

306
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:06,539
Hello, Manager.

307
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,000
What?

308
00:20:28,144 --> 00:20:29,812
This punk's not answering his phone.

309
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,231
Hey, Park Gi-tae.

310
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:33,733
Mr. Yang.

311
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,693
What are you doing right now?

312
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,696
They asked me to move these.

313
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:41,198
Who the fuck did?
The buying department?

314
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:47,580
Mr. Yang.

315
00:20:48,539 --> 00:20:49,540
Mr. Yang!

316
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,391
Where's Mr. Kang?

317
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:10,811
Where is Mr. Kang?

318
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:15,524
Yes, how may I help you?

319
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:17,902
I'm from Hongsung's Sales Division.

320
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:22,156
Did your team tell my staff
to haul boxes?

321
00:21:23,449 --> 00:21:25,074
He offered to do it.

322
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,827
Or did I mishear him?

323
00:21:27,578 --> 00:21:30,955
Are you playing games with us
over the Aileye contract?

324
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:34,083
Moving a few boxes
won't solve the contract issue.

325
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:36,128
What an odd thing to say.

326
00:21:36,796 --> 00:21:38,463
- Hey, Park Gi-tae.
- Yes.

327
00:21:38,464 --> 00:21:40,382
Tell me exactly what happened.

328
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:45,888
Well, Mr. Kang said
he'd consider the contract renewal

329
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:48,307
and asked me
to help organize the boxes.

330
00:21:48,766 --> 00:21:50,976
And that guy over there

331
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:53,729
moved a couple of boxes
and then disappeared.

332
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,314
Is that true?

333
00:21:56,607 --> 00:21:57,690
Well, yes.

334
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,984
But I didn't do it on purpose.

335
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:02,071
- I just...
- Are you still denying it?

336
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:06,325
Why are you coming at me?
I have no power.

337
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:10,578
The contract renewal is
the general manager's decision.

338
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:11,663
Exactly.

339
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:12,872
So I'm asking

340
00:22:12,873 --> 00:22:15,792
why a powerless bastard like you
is fucking around with us!

341
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:16,876
"Fucking around"?

342
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,253
You piece of shit.

343
00:22:18,254 --> 00:22:20,296
- Hey, come here!
- Sir, please...

344
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,381
Come at me, motherfucker.

345
00:22:21,382 --> 00:22:23,091
Who the hell are you
to order me around?

346
00:22:23,092 --> 00:22:25,678
Let me go.
Do you hear what this punk is saying?

347
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:28,722
That scumbag still thinks
he holds the power.

348
00:22:28,973 --> 00:22:31,266
Then do you hold the power?
Are you CGM?

349
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:33,643
A little shit like you
throws your weight around?

350
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:35,228
What a damn lunatic.

351
00:22:35,229 --> 00:22:38,232
We were going to spare
a few of your stores, but forget it.

352
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:41,025
Get rid of all your stores,
you fucking bastard!

353
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,819
Who are you to decide that?

354
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:44,612
Don't spare them, you fucking idiot.

355
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:46,114
Damn it, I can't take this.

356
00:22:46,115 --> 00:22:47,323
- Let go.
- Damn what?

357
00:22:47,324 --> 00:22:48,575
I said, let me go!

358
00:22:48,576 --> 00:22:50,286
- So what? Try me!
- You little...

359
00:22:50,536 --> 00:22:51,912
Hit me, you motherfucker!

360
00:22:52,162 --> 00:22:53,163
Go ahead!

361
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:55,874
Hey, forget it.

362
00:22:55,875 --> 00:22:57,293
Just get out of my sight.

363
00:22:57,543 --> 00:22:59,419
I don't care
about your business anymore

364
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:00,838
- so get lost!
- Hey.

365
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:03,549
I'll leave even if you freaking
beg me to stay.

366
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:05,175
Let's go.

367
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:07,677
One more thing.

368
00:23:07,678 --> 00:23:09,804
You should call your mother
and apologize.

369
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:11,223
Say sorry for being a disappointment.

370
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:12,892
Do you understand?

371
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:16,437
You're nothing
but a pathetic fucking loser.

372
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,274
What a piece of shit.

373
00:23:21,692 --> 00:23:23,444
The power dynamic in this industry
always changes.

374
00:23:23,694 --> 00:23:24,987
Don't regret it when the time comes.

375
00:23:25,237 --> 00:23:26,530
Remember, you started it.

376
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,577
Jeez, what an asshole.

377
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:34,163
Gosh, that little...

378
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:40,084
Why would you just do
what that punk told you to do?

379
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,252
I'm sorry.

380
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:43,213
Moving boxes won't resolve
the contract issue.

381
00:23:43,631 --> 00:23:44,964
Let's say it actually does.

382
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,759
That's even more ridiculous.

383
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:49,678
Will you just keep moving boxes?

384
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:54,557
This wasn't just you
moving boxes as an individual.

385
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,601
It was Paradi Mall
using Hongsung International

386
00:23:56,602 --> 00:23:58,145
as their lackeys.

387
00:23:58,812 --> 00:23:59,813
Do you get that?

388
00:24:00,981 --> 00:24:03,567
I'm sorry, sir.
I didn't think that far.

389
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:06,904
You drive, punk.

390
00:24:07,696 --> 00:24:09,198
- Yes, sir.
- Jeez.

391
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:18,539
Hello, I'm Mo Yu-jin
of INA Mall's Sales Team.

392
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:20,167
- Yes, hello.
- Hello.

393
00:24:20,918 --> 00:24:21,919
Have a seat.

394
00:24:25,047 --> 00:24:26,256
Wait, 20%?

395
00:24:27,049 --> 00:24:29,968
Yes, as I just told you,
20% for luxury stores

396
00:24:29,969 --> 00:24:31,887
and 36% for regular stores.

397
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:34,556
You're raising it by 4% so suddenly?

398
00:24:35,057 --> 00:24:36,850
We're not just doing this
to Hongsung.

399
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:40,020
Will these margins also apply to CGM?

400
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:42,147
Yes.

401
00:24:43,607 --> 00:24:45,651
You're basically telling us
to close our stores.

402
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,863
Well, if you can't do it,
then that's too bad.

403
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:53,325
What if we accept your terms?

404
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:55,452
Will you raise it to 22%?

405
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:59,373
That's very likely
if Hongsung and CGM both accept.

406
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:02,126
What will you do if we back out?

407
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:03,627
Will you pay the penalty?

408
00:25:04,461 --> 00:25:07,006
Yes, we intend to pay the penalty.

409
00:25:07,798 --> 00:25:10,050
The contract renewal is
just six months away.

410
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:12,553
But you'd rather pay the penalty?

411
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:16,390
That's what we've decided to do.

412
00:25:17,683 --> 00:25:19,601
May I speak to your team leader?

413
00:25:22,563 --> 00:25:26,358
They sent me,
which is why Hongsung sent you, no?

414
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,359
If my team leader came

415
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,029
then I'm sure
you would have sent yours as well.

416
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:33,489
They want us assistant managers
to handle it ourselves.

417
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:34,533
Don't you get that?

418
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,119
I have to go now.

419
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:39,579
Let me know when you make a decision.

420
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:42,040
I'll give you until next week.

421
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,834
All right, then. Take care.

422
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:52,467
You did well.

423
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:54,093
I would've done the same thing.

424
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:55,763
Oh, not at all.

425
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:57,930
I shouldn't have gone that far.

426
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:59,725
But I was so angry at the moment.

427
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:01,852
I'm sorry, sir.

428
00:26:02,478 --> 00:26:04,855
How many times will you apologize?

429
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:06,815
I'm sorry... I mean, sorry...

430
00:26:07,149 --> 00:26:08,150
Enough.

431
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:12,738
Over here.

432
00:26:13,322 --> 00:26:14,405
The food's still warm.

433
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:15,573
- Hello.
- We ordered for you.

434
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:17,533
- Good work today.
- Good work, everyone.

435
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,036
Good work, you two. Eat up.

436
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:23,457
Nice work, Mr. Yang.

437
00:26:23,916 --> 00:26:24,917
What do you mean?

438
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,794
Word has already gotten around.

439
00:26:27,795 --> 00:26:30,505
Mr. Yang of Hongsung
called Mr. Kang of Paradi Mall

440
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:33,133
"a pathetic fucking loser."

441
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,177
Is that all they're saying?

442
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:39,347
- Not how I verbally destroyed him?
- No.

443
00:26:39,348 --> 00:26:42,351
They're just saying you called him
a pathetic fucking loser.

444
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:44,728
Damn, that sucks.

445
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:50,817
So are they asking for 20%?

446
00:26:50,818 --> 00:26:52,277
Well, yes.

447
00:26:53,195 --> 00:26:55,697
I've never heard of anyone
asking for 20% in Korea.

448
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:58,032
Did CGM really accept those terms?

449
00:26:58,033 --> 00:26:59,450
Will they even make a profit?

450
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,620
Exactly, I doubt they will.

451
00:27:02,329 --> 00:27:03,996
If anything, they'd lose money.

452
00:27:03,997 --> 00:27:06,290
Same with the mall employees.
It makes no sense.

453
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:08,209
Contract renewals are in six months.

454
00:27:08,210 --> 00:27:10,294
Why would they pay the penalty?

455
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:13,632
They're willing to overextend
to increase market power short-term.

456
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:15,259
Why?

457
00:27:15,509 --> 00:27:18,011
They could easily beat us
even if they took their time.

458
00:27:21,473 --> 00:27:23,558
Ji-hye, are you trading crypto
or something?

459
00:27:23,559 --> 00:27:25,602
Sorry, sir.
I just have to send this one thing.

460
00:27:25,936 --> 00:27:29,063
- What is it?
- Laknes sent next season's designs.

461
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,774
I have to share it with Marketing.

462
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:32,400
- I see.
- Show us.

463
00:27:32,401 --> 00:27:34,026
I understand if it's Laknes.

464
00:27:34,027 --> 00:27:36,029
- Should I send it to all of you?
- Yes, please do.

465
00:27:37,823 --> 00:27:38,824
Okay, I sent it.

466
00:27:43,579 --> 00:27:44,955
These designs are intense.

467
00:27:45,581 --> 00:27:47,166
I don't get the style these days.

468
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:48,916
Isn't it too out there?

469
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:51,920
The extreme designs
sell well in China.

470
00:27:52,254 --> 00:27:53,796
That's true.

471
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:56,341
These days, you've got to sell well
in China before anything else.

472
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:11,481
- Mr. Gong.
- Wait.

473
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:14,401
- Mr. Yang, Mr. Gong!
- Mr. Gong.

474
00:28:15,319 --> 00:28:16,402
Mr. Yang!

475
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:19,156
NAENGMYEON AND BULGOGI PLATTERS

476
00:28:20,949 --> 00:28:21,950
Mr. Yang!

477
00:28:22,743 --> 00:28:23,910
Mr. Gong!

478
00:28:23,911 --> 00:28:25,245
- Where are they going?
- Mr. Gong.

479
00:28:27,789 --> 00:28:29,416
Ms. Joo resigned today.

480
00:28:30,626 --> 00:28:32,085
Unsurprising, right?

481
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:36,756
Over five people have resigned
from Sales Division 1.

482
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:38,966
Team 1's Park Eun-sik also quit.

483
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:40,010
Park Eun-sik?

484
00:28:41,261 --> 00:28:43,221
They even took a rookie like him?

485
00:28:43,222 --> 00:28:45,849
Well, he claims he's quitting
due to a family issue.

486
00:28:46,475 --> 00:28:47,892
After what happened last time

487
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:50,645
we did our best to crack down.
I can't believe this.

488
00:28:50,646 --> 00:28:52,563
Last time was an ethical issue.

489
00:28:52,564 --> 00:28:54,066
This time is a bit different.

490
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:57,319
Who can stop them
from pursuing better benefits?

491
00:28:57,903 --> 00:28:58,904
Even so

492
00:28:59,238 --> 00:29:02,449
they should tell us honestly,
instead of claiming family issues.

493
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:05,326
All right, that's enough.

494
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:06,869
Let's forget about those who left.

495
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,705
Let them go. We have work to do.

496
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:12,959
Any new developments
since the last report?

497
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,710
Not yet

498
00:29:14,711 --> 00:29:16,672
but I have a feeling
there will be soon.

499
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:19,465
All right.

500
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:22,802
If any more brands or partners
want to terminate contracts

501
00:29:22,803 --> 00:29:24,721
don't stop them. Just report it.

502
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:27,515
I'm sure some haven't said anything
out of morality.

503
00:29:27,516 --> 00:29:28,767
There will definitely be more.

504
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:31,812
And don't be meek
when dealing with the malls.

505
00:29:33,397 --> 00:29:37,149
But if we don't try to stop them,
we'll lose 50% of our brands

506
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:39,069
and 60% of our retailers.

507
00:29:40,362 --> 00:29:41,530
Then what should we do?

508
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:44,032
Should we beg them to stay?

509
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:46,326
Won't that just make us look bad?

510
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:48,912
No need to blame them.

511
00:29:49,705 --> 00:29:52,832
Ultimately, a company
must make a profit.

512
00:29:52,833 --> 00:29:56,836
If someone offered me a better deal,
I'd take it too.

513
00:29:56,837 --> 00:29:58,379
Did you think they were our friends

514
00:29:58,380 --> 00:30:00,507
because we always shook hands
and ate good meals together?

515
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:02,509
There's no such thing here.

516
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:06,179
The world runs
on that kind of hypocrisy.

517
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:07,888
Right now

518
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:10,434
that hypocrisy just feels
a bit harsher.

519
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:12,811
It'll be tough for a while

520
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:15,187
but our company
won't go under from this.

521
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,189
Have confidence.

522
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:18,316
While we're at it

523
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:20,860
take everything we moved
to shopping complexes and outlets

524
00:30:20,861 --> 00:30:22,278
back to the malls.

525
00:30:22,279 --> 00:30:24,031
- Revert them to full price.
- Yes, ma'am.

526
00:30:24,323 --> 00:30:27,117
Does this mean we're giving up
on inventory management?

527
00:30:27,576 --> 00:30:29,161
We can't manage
the inventory, anyway.

528
00:30:29,578 --> 00:30:32,331
At times like this, we should try
to get the penalty fees.

529
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:39,546
TEAM 5 LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

530
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:43,884
Yes, what is it?

531
00:30:50,891 --> 00:30:52,684
- Hello, Ms. Park.
- Hello, ma'am.

532
00:30:53,685 --> 00:30:54,894
What is this about?

533
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:56,063
What about CGM?

534
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:58,482
It's China.

535
00:30:58,899 --> 00:31:00,317
- Because of tariffs?
- Yes.

536
00:31:00,776 --> 00:31:04,529
Laknes also entered the Korean market
because of tariffs, didn't it?

537
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:08,075
If they deliver to China from Korea,
they can avoid tariffs.

538
00:31:09,034 --> 00:31:11,077
Look, I get the logic.

539
00:31:11,078 --> 00:31:12,746
But it still makes no sense.

540
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:15,123
Why would they go this far?

541
00:31:16,124 --> 00:31:18,001
There's a rumor
going around Shenzhen.

542
00:31:18,377 --> 00:31:19,627
Starting next year

543
00:31:19,628 --> 00:31:21,545
new company establishment

544
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:23,715
will be heavily restricted
in Shenzhen's tax-free zone

545
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:25,926
That's only three months away.

546
00:31:26,343 --> 00:31:29,470
Yes, they must register their company
in Korea and China

547
00:31:29,471 --> 00:31:30,888
secure distribution centers

548
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:31,972
make initial shipments

549
00:31:31,973 --> 00:31:34,183
and generate sales before then.

550
00:31:34,184 --> 00:31:37,478
Shenzhen grants tariff exemption
only once sales are generated.

551
00:31:37,479 --> 00:31:39,021
So once it becomes next year

552
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:41,483
CGM won't be able to receive
tariff exemption.

553
00:31:42,526 --> 00:31:43,568
Have you verified this?

554
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:46,154
I checked with Shenzhen's
Deputy Secretary's assistant.

555
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:48,990
We can win if we drag this out.

556
00:31:49,783 --> 00:31:50,784
He's right.

557
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:53,244
If we compete with CGM

558
00:31:53,245 --> 00:31:55,746
and pretend to fight
while raising the margin rate

559
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:57,374
CGM won't be able to hang on.

560
00:31:57,749 --> 00:32:00,334
If they can't enter China's market,
there's no need for them

561
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:02,462
to take on such margin rates
in Korea.

562
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:07,884
There's another option
besides dragging this out.

563
00:32:08,552 --> 00:32:10,137
What? You're making me nervous.

564
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:11,680
What is it?

565
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:15,517
Let's start with making back
our penalty fees.

566
00:32:35,412 --> 00:32:38,081
Why are these punks so confident?

567
00:32:38,665 --> 00:32:40,958
No, we understand your position.

568
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:45,464
We can only proceed with CGM.
I hope you understand.

569
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:48,257
Then we'll immediately withdraw
all of our retailers

570
00:32:48,258 --> 00:32:49,384
upon contract termination.

571
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:51,427
I hope you know it'll be very hard

572
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:53,805
to generate this level of revenue
in the future.

573
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:56,057
Damn it.

574
00:32:58,226 --> 00:32:59,227
Don't mind me.

575
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:02,522
I'll take that.

576
00:33:02,856 --> 00:33:04,107
It's okay. Give it to me.

577
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,611
What a load of nonsense.

578
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:11,780
Have you made a decision?

579
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:12,782
Yes.

580
00:33:13,283 --> 00:33:14,868
We'll clear out all our stores.

581
00:33:15,911 --> 00:33:16,994
Sorry?

582
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:19,080
We just can't accept a 4% increase.

583
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:22,416
- But...
- As for the penalty fee

584
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:25,003
our legal team will be in touch.
Goodbye, then.

585
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:32,010
What was that?

586
00:33:33,136 --> 00:33:34,720
After taking care of the penalties

587
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:37,473
Hongsung will enter
the Chinese market before CGM.

588
00:33:37,474 --> 00:33:39,267
We've already expanded to China.

589
00:33:39,559 --> 00:33:41,477
Yes, but our China branch
is practically

590
00:33:41,478 --> 00:33:43,687
just a distribution channel
for Korean brands.

591
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:44,772
So?

592
00:33:44,773 --> 00:33:46,942
You suggest we bring
foreign brands to China first?

593
00:33:47,192 --> 00:33:48,275
Yes, sir.

594
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:51,153
We'll select the ones
CGM is most afraid of

595
00:33:51,154 --> 00:33:54,241
and Hongsung will plant our flag
in China before CGM does.

596
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:56,159
Is that even possible?

597
00:33:56,701 --> 00:34:00,121
Would global brands
even want to team up with us

598
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:02,457
over CGM?

599
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:05,085
Maybe not if it was
between us and CGM.

600
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:08,547
But what about Mantua?

601
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:22,810
CGM may be an industry giant

602
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:24,645
but they can't compare to Mantua.

603
00:34:24,646 --> 00:34:27,064
Honestly,
if we just look at perfume sales

604
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:29,067
Mantua is in a whole different class.

605
00:34:29,526 --> 00:34:32,112
CGM's brands may do well
in North America

606
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:35,782
but Mantua has European brands
expanding worldwide.

607
00:34:38,201 --> 00:34:40,202
They just dump inventory wholesale.

608
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:41,412
Will they consider retail?

609
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:44,916
What if we set everything up in China
so they can sell wholesale?

610
00:34:45,417 --> 00:34:48,377
It's not like Hongsung is saying
we'll be their agency.

611
00:34:48,378 --> 00:34:52,172
It's a win-win strategy
if they just help us secure brands.

612
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:53,466
There's no reason not to do it.

613
00:34:53,717 --> 00:34:57,929
If they do it, Mantua's brands
will wholly become ours.

614
00:34:58,555 --> 00:34:59,556
He's right.

615
00:34:59,889 --> 00:35:02,225
In a fight between CGM and Mantua

616
00:35:02,892 --> 00:35:05,436
- no brand would join CGM.
- Right.

617
00:35:05,437 --> 00:35:07,646
If we can bring Mantua to China

618
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:09,399
we will win.

619
00:35:09,858 --> 00:35:13,194
So we'll get the penalties we're owed
and win this futile fight too.

620
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:15,238
And those who left us

621
00:35:15,655 --> 00:35:18,115
will have no choice
but to renew contracts with us.

622
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,619
Yes, we can get even better terms.

623
00:35:25,624 --> 00:35:26,791
This conversation

624
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:28,585
must stay between us.

625
00:35:31,004 --> 00:35:32,087
Park Gi-tae, Lee Ji-hye.

626
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:33,172
- Yes?
- Yes?

627
00:35:33,173 --> 00:35:34,633
You two should be most careful.

628
00:35:35,008 --> 00:35:37,844
People tend to spill when they
suddenly get exclusive information.

629
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:39,429
Do you understand?

630
00:35:40,013 --> 00:35:41,348
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, we'll be careful.

631
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:44,391
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes?

632
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:47,478
Starting tomorrow, withdraw from
all stores requesting new contracts

633
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:48,647
and collect the penalty fees.

634
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:52,108
- Interior construction costs too.
- Yes, ma'am.

635
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:53,734
And Mr. Gong.

636
00:35:53,735 --> 00:35:56,529
Do whatever it takes
to get Sponza on board.

637
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:58,156
That's our lifeline.

638
00:35:58,531 --> 00:35:59,574
Yes, ma'am.

639
00:36:01,910 --> 00:36:03,036
Let's call it a day.

640
00:36:10,126 --> 00:36:11,670
Ms. Park has such an aura.

641
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:14,172
Ms. Park knows my name.

642
00:36:14,673 --> 00:36:15,674
Mine too.

643
00:36:16,132 --> 00:36:19,343
Hey, Ms. Park knows me
better than I know myself.

644
00:36:19,344 --> 00:36:21,221
I bet she knows you all
better than you know yourselves.

645
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:22,972
Hurry up.

646
00:36:32,065 --> 00:36:33,191
All right.

647
00:36:43,702 --> 00:36:44,744
Here we are.

648
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:46,620
This dish is

649
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:49,958
roe, caviar, and truffle
atop grilled blackthroat seaperch.

650
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:52,419
Wait, I'll set it down for you.

651
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:56,172
Thank you, sir.

652
00:36:56,631 --> 00:36:58,006
Eat the roe first.

653
00:36:58,007 --> 00:36:59,843
Then the caviar and the truffle.

654
00:37:00,093 --> 00:37:01,094
All right.

655
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:07,766
How is it?

656
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:09,018
Wow, it's incredible.

657
00:37:12,814 --> 00:37:13,815
Thank you.

658
00:37:18,445 --> 00:37:21,406
Hongsung says
they'll withdraw all their stores.

659
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:25,118
At this rate,
my mall will be full of empty spots.

660
00:37:25,827 --> 00:37:28,245
We'll fill those spots
with even better terms.

661
00:37:28,246 --> 00:37:29,456
Why are you worrying?

662
00:37:30,165 --> 00:37:32,083
Change is a scary thing.

663
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:34,919
Even more so
when there's no resistance to it.

664
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:37,797
Sir.

665
00:37:39,591 --> 00:37:41,301
You have nothing to worry about.

666
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:43,511
Hongsung has no cards to play.

667
00:37:43,970 --> 00:37:46,180
That's what makes it weirder.

668
00:37:46,181 --> 00:37:49,476
I assumed they'd at least accept 20%.

669
00:37:51,394 --> 00:37:53,980
They probably figure
contract renewal won't be easy

670
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:56,483
and are trying to get
their penalty fees instead.

671
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:59,194
Of course, they'll try to get
their penalty fees.

672
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:01,863
But I saw it's not just us.

673
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:04,031
It looks like they're withdrawing

674
00:38:04,032 --> 00:38:05,742
from every mall
that requested a new contract.

675
00:38:07,202 --> 00:38:10,413
This means Hongsung
is getting out of the business.

676
00:38:11,039 --> 00:38:12,415
They should, if they can't handle it.

677
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:13,917
What else can they do?

678
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:19,589
- Mr. Jeong.
- Yes?

679
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:21,382
How long were you at Hongsung?

680
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:23,259
Eleven years.

681
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:25,261
During that time

682
00:38:25,887 --> 00:38:27,639
how many crises did Hongsung face?

683
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:30,266
I'm not sure.

684
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:35,313
Hongsung won't fall this easily.

685
00:38:36,064 --> 00:38:37,732
I know that better than you.

686
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:42,612
I admire your confidence

687
00:38:43,071 --> 00:38:44,572
but don't get too complacent.

688
00:38:45,490 --> 00:38:48,535
If things go wrong,
we'll be taking a big hit.

689
00:38:49,202 --> 00:38:50,912
Yes, sir. I understand.

690
00:39:01,548 --> 00:39:02,714
NOAVILLA MALL
CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE

691
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,384
DELMAR MALL
CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE

692
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:09,305
VICE PRESIDENT KOO IN-MOCK

693
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:14,310
Come in.

694
00:39:23,403 --> 00:39:24,404
You wanted to see me, sir?

695
00:39:29,284 --> 00:39:30,285
What is all this?

696
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:33,454
We can't resolve this
by clinging to them.

697
00:39:34,289 --> 00:39:35,665
So you'll withdraw from everything?

698
00:39:36,791 --> 00:39:38,668
Do you just want to shut down
without a plan?

699
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:41,170
We have a plan, sir.

700
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:42,422
What is it?

701
00:39:43,715 --> 00:39:45,007
I'm sorry for asking

702
00:39:45,008 --> 00:39:46,843
but may I report to you
at a later date?

703
00:39:50,013 --> 00:39:52,222
You punk, what do you take me for?

704
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:54,600
Jeong Seon-hyuk offered
our Finance Team's leader

705
00:39:54,601 --> 00:39:57,562
the CFO position
for CGM's Korea Branch.

706
00:39:58,396 --> 00:40:00,981
- So?
- If I were Jeong Seon-hyuk

707
00:40:00,982 --> 00:40:04,152
the first person I would contact
would be you, Mr. Koo.

708
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:07,946
Even if he meets
with the malls as CEO

709
00:40:07,947 --> 00:40:09,907
they'll still talk down to him

710
00:40:09,908 --> 00:40:12,535
because he's still the same person,
even with CGM backing him.

711
00:40:13,369 --> 00:40:15,914
If he wants to talk with the malls
on equal footing

712
00:40:16,456 --> 00:40:18,499
he needs someone like you,
don't you think?

713
00:40:19,959 --> 00:40:22,587
So are you keeping it confidential
even from me?

714
00:40:24,172 --> 00:40:25,214
I'm sorry, sir.

715
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:37,870
Mr. Gong Eun-tae?

716
00:41:57,098 --> 00:42:02,020
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

717
00:42:15,116 --> 00:42:18,286
TEAM 5 LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

718
00:42:18,953 --> 00:42:20,204
Yes, what is it?

719
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:33,634
MY DAUGHTER

720
00:42:36,471 --> 00:42:37,889
MOM

721
00:42:42,894 --> 00:42:44,561
Hi, Mom. Where are you?

722
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:46,354
Yun-gyeong, are you at home?

723
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:47,481
Where else would I be?

724
00:42:47,482 --> 00:42:48,649
You wanted to eat dinner together.

725
00:42:49,317 --> 00:42:50,318
Right.

726
00:42:51,069 --> 00:42:53,988
But I think I'll be a little late.

727
00:42:54,614 --> 00:42:55,615
Unbelievable.

728
00:42:56,449 --> 00:42:58,910
I told you
I was just going to eat with Min-ji.

729
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:00,410
I'm sorry.

730
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:02,537
I planned to get home early

731
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:03,790
- but something came up...
- Whatever.

732
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:05,666
Did I beg you to eat with me?

733
00:43:06,042 --> 00:43:07,709
Why make a promise you can't keep?

734
00:43:07,710 --> 00:43:09,669
So annoying.

735
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:11,338
And it's my birthday. Seriously?

736
00:43:11,339 --> 00:43:14,217
Well, I really was trying
to get home early.

737
00:43:14,759 --> 00:43:16,176
Whatever, I'm going out.

738
00:43:16,177 --> 00:43:17,469
Where?

739
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:19,513
Start eating with Dad.
I'll be there soon.

740
00:43:19,514 --> 00:43:21,431
Why would I eat with Dad?

741
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:22,433
I'm hanging up.

742
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:41,994
WHEN TURNING LEFT,
YIELD TO PEDESTRIANS

743
00:46:19,944 --> 00:46:21,904
Subtitles by Eunice Kim
